From 28002b97495d151e1516993f0bb074228d3d4cb5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Christian F.K. Schaller" <christian.schaller@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 15:10:08 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] scanner: Hand the session's first reference to its close

This commit stops OpenScanner from dropping the reference it created
the session with. xdp_session_close () ends by dropping one reference
more than export and register took, which is that one, as the other
portals that make sessions rely on. Dropping it at the end of the call
as well left the helper's exit callback as the only other holder, so
closing the session freed it under the callback, which then locked the
scanner's mutex through a freed session and crashed the portal.

Found while building the frontend on xdg-desktop-portal 1.22.1, where
it crashed in the scenario that closes a session by leaving the bus.
The frontend on main did not crash in the same run.

Tested: the scenario checks pass 40 of 40 on main and on 1.22.1.
---
 desktop-portal/scanner.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/desktop-portal/scanner.c b/desktop-portal/scanner.c
index e132b2d..736c6e7 100644
--- a/desktop-portal/scanner.c
+++ b/desktop-portal/scanner.c
@@ -1024,6 +1024,10 @@ handle_open_scanner (XdpDbusScanner         *object,
 
   xdp_dbus_scanner_complete_open_scanner (object, invocation, XDP_SESSION (session)->id);
 
+  /* xdp_session_close () drops one more reference than export and register took, the one this
+   * call was created with, so it is not released here. */
+  g_steal_pointer (&session);
+
   return G_DBUS_METHOD_INVOCATION_HANDLED;
 }
 
